00:31:02.486 --> 00:31:03.671
Well.
I'm not saying you're wrong.

495
00:31:03.695 --> 00:31:07.290
I'm just saying that maybe
there are other possibilities.

496
00:31:09.201 --> 00:31:12.041
When it killed Sean. I knew with
absolute certainty it had come for him-

497
00:31:12.079 --> 00:31:13.456
I knew that!

498
00:31:14.706 --> 00:31:16.458
I know it's coming.

499
00:31:17.667 --> 00:31:19.419
I know it's coming.

500
00:31:22.422 --> 00:31:24.174
What's it cost to take
a ride on that plane?

501
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:27.553
The water's coming in!
The water's coming in!

502
00:31:28.637 --> 00:31:30.355
Depends on where you want to go.

503
00:31:30.722 --> 00:31:31.769
Doesn't matter.

504
00:31:31.848 --> 00:31:33.316
Hurry!

505
00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:34.600
Just like that?

506
00:31:34.643 --> 00:31:36.361
Just like that.

507
00:31:36.478 --> 00:31:40.699
Oh! Oh. no! Oh! Oh!

508
00:31:42.609 --> 00:31:43.610
Take the wheel!

509
00:31:43.693 --> 00:31:45.036
I'm sorry.
What did you say?

510
00:31:45.112 --> 00:31:46.739
Take the wheel.

511
00:31:46.988 --> 00:31:48.410
No. I can't.
Sure. you can.

512
00:31:48.490 --> 00:31:49.958
No. I mean. I...
I don't know how.

513
00:31:50.033 --> 00:31:52.161
Nobody does till they learn.

514
00:31:56.331 --> 00:31:57.378
What are you doing?

515
00:31:57.457 --> 00:32:00.256
You better take the wheel or we'll
be swimming in five minutes.

516
00:32:01.002 --> 00:32:03.346
Whoa. take it easy!
Take it easy!

517
00:32:04.339 --> 00:32:06.808
Hold her gently.
She'll damn near fly herself.

518
00:32:13.348 --> 00:32:15.442
See? Just like driving a car.

519
00:32:15.517 --> 00:32:16.661
Where do I pull off the road?

520
00:32:16.685 --> 00:32:18.687
No. you're doing fine.

521
00:32:19.062 --> 00:32:21.235
I'll keep you out of trouble.

522
00:32:21.857 --> 00:32:23.029
Relax.

523
00:32:23.900 --> 00:32:24.992
Where are we going?

524
00:32:25.068 --> 00:32:27.662
One time. I was flying
supplies up the Amazon

525
00:32:27.737 --> 00:32:30.035
when I came down in the jungle.

526
00:32:30.115 --> 00:32:31.175
You're not gonna
tell me. are you?

527
00:32:31.199 --> 00:32:32.844
I was picked up by this
tribe of head-hunters.

528
00:32:32.868 --> 00:32:34.461
and they took me
to see their chief.

529
00:32:34.536 --> 00:32:35.536
You are impossible!

530
00:32:35.579 --> 00:32:37.047
He took a long look at me

531
00:32:37.581 --> 00:32:39.128
and he took me in his hut.

532
00:32:39.207 --> 00:32:41.209
Inside his hut.
there was a long pole...

533
00:32:57.142 --> 00:32:58.564
What is all this?

534
00:32:58.643 --> 00:33:01.146
Just a little something
I arranged to cheer you up.

535
00:33:01.229 --> 00:33:02.230
No. really.

536
00:33:02.397 --> 00:33:03.398
What?

537
00:33:03.565 --> 00:33:05.408
Tell me. what is all this?

538
00:33:05.484 --> 00:33:06.827
It's a local festival.

539
00:33:06.902 --> 00:33:08.745
It's called a Junkanoo.

540
00:33:11.490 --> 00:33:12.992
Yeah. <i>I</i>
tell you. I'm not... I'm not

541
00:33:13.074 --> 00:33:14.496
<i>hearing anything up here. buddy.</i>

542
00:33:14.576 --> 00:33:17.830
How many have you tagged. exacfly?
How many?

543
00:33:18.413 --> 00:33:22.168
Michael.
stop busting my bunghie.

544
00:33:23.585 --> 00:33:26.088
Yeah. it's okay for you.
but not for me. huh?

545
00:33:26.546 --> 00:33:28.640
Have no fear. Jake is here.

546
00:33:28.757 --> 00:33:31.681
I just struck the mother lode.
I'm counting.

547
00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:33.762
<i>You better watch
yourself with that fancy</i>

548
00:33:33.929 --> 00:33:35.681
<i>electrical
equipment down there. buddy.</i>

549
00:33:36.097 --> 00:33:38.367
Such a live wire is liable to
make your hair stick up funny.

550
00:33:38.391 --> 00:33:41.065
That's good. Michael.
William?

551
00:33:41.394 --> 00:33:42.754
Yeah.
there's no hope for that boy.

552
00:33:43.855 --> 00:33:46.950
Jake? Jake. that's a joke.

553
00:33:50.070 --> 00:33:51.447
Holy shit!

554
00:33:56.535 --> 00:33:58.162
We got a big
fish down here. man.

555
00:33:59.204 --> 00:34:00.877
Oh. yeah? How big?

556
00:34:02.624 --> 00:34:03.841
Jesus!
Look out!

557
00:34:05.585 --> 00:34:07.258
Shit!
Look out!

558
00:34:11.132 --> 00:34:12.258
What's wrong?

559
00:34:16.346 --> 00:34:17.518
Ellen?

560
00:34:21.768 --> 00:34:23.736
Jesus Christ!

561
00:34:28.108 --> 00:34:29.200
<i>Ellen. what's wrong?</i>

562
00:34:29.985 --> 00:34:32.283
Nothing. Nothing. I'm fine.

563
00:34:33.113 --> 00:34:34.160
No. you're not.

564
00:34:34.239 --> 00:34:35.411
I'm terrific.

565
00:34:43.832 --> 00:34:45.084
Come on!

566
00:34:47.419 --> 00:34:48.796
Give it up!

567
00:34:50.505 --> 00:34:51.927
You can't keep doing this.

568
00:34:52.674 --> 00:34:54.768
I can't keep doing this.

569
00:34:54.843 --> 00:34:56.220
Hey. you promised me a drink.

570
00:34:56.720 --> 00:34:58.848
Sharks come and go. Ellen.

571
00:34:59.014 --> 00:35:00.812
People have got
nothing to do with it.

572
00:35:00.890 --> 00:35:02.437
A drink with an umbrella in it.

573
00:35:03.310 --> 00:35:05.984
Ellen. give it up.

574
00:35:07.564 --> 00:35:09.783
Give it a kick in the ass.

575
00:35:09.899 --> 00:35:11.242
Get on with your life.

576
00:35:19.868 --> 00:35:21.370
I know what you've been through.

577
00:35:21.453 --> 00:35:24.127
Don't worry.
The nightmares'll go away.

578
00:35:29.794 --> 00:35:31.717
Give me my glasses. man.

579
00:35:32.589 --> 00:35:35.012
Boy. I ain't never
seen nothin' so big. Never!

580
00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:36.802
I was standin'
right next to Michael.

581
00:35:36.885 --> 00:35:38.558
The blasted thing
went right past me!

582
00:35:38.637 --> 00:35:40.685
Should've gone for you. Jake.
It was right over you.

583
00:35:40.764 --> 00:35:41.811
Why did it come up?

584
00:35:41.890 --> 00:35:43.576
What the hell's it doing
in warm water anyway. man?

585
00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:45.523
What's the difference. man?
It's here.

586
00:35:45.602 --> 00:35:47.525
It's only a shark. A great.
big. beautiful shark.

587
00:35:47.604 --> 00:35:49.404
You two are makin' it
into somethin' it's not.

588
00:35:49.648 --> 00:35:51.901
And it's ours. Don't say
anything to anyone. man.

589
00:35:51.983 --> 00:35:54.712
Fishermen find out. they're gonna try
to kill it first thing you know. huh?

590
00:35:54.736 --> 00:35:57.159
Michael.
we got us a great white.

591
00:35:57.238 --> 00:35:59.787
Now. we gonna do some
real research. boy.

592
00:36:00.408 --> 00:36:04.413
Do me a favor. will you? Don't... Don't
say anything about this to my mom.

593
00:36:05.955 --> 00:36:09.459
Hey. man. I didn't mean to.
you know. flap my lips. eh?

594
00:36:33.608 --> 00:36:35.451
- So...
- SO?

595
00:36:36.778 --> 00:36:39.531
I said to him.
"Where's the disinfectant?"

596
00:36:44.202 --> 00:36:46.250
He said.
"I've left it in town."

597
00:36:46.329 --> 00:36:48.798
So I said.
"What are we gonna do?"

598
00:36:49.207 --> 00:36:52.177
So he says.
"I'll tell you what we'll do.

599
00:36:54.087 --> 00:36:57.136
"Come back at lunchtime. all the
flies will be in the kitchen."

600
00:37:00.009 --> 00:37:01.181
Come to bed.

601
00:37:05.098 --> 00:37:06.566
He took her sightseeing.

602
00:37:08.101 --> 00:37:10.229
Well. you work. I work.

603
00:37:10.311 --> 00:37:14.157
I mean. she needs someone to help
her take her mind off things.

604
00:37:28.163 --> 00:37:30.962
I'll help you take your
mind off things. sailor.

605
00:37:43.636 --> 00:37:45.104
It's soaking.

606
00:37:48.349 --> 00:37:49.692
Thank you.

607
00:37:52.729 --> 00:37:54.106
Good night.

608
00:37:58.902 --> 00:38:00.279
Good night.

609
00:38:21.049 --> 00:38:22.517
Five minutes.

610
00:38:22.884 --> 00:38:23.885
Louisa.

611
00:38:23.968 --> 00:38:26.972
It's okay. It's all right. Jake.
I'll check on the table.

612
00:38:29.098 --> 00:38:31.476
Okay. Okay. everything
rides-Everything rides.

613
00:38:31.559 --> 00:38:33.061
Ooh. hey. it's Hoagie!

614
00:38:33.144 --> 00:38:35.146
Hey. come on. I wanna see this.

615
00:38:35.772 --> 00:38:37.240
Oh. that's Hoagie. all right.

616
00:38:41.361 --> 00:38:43.409
Everything on the line.

617
00:38:43.738 --> 00:38:45.174
You're not...
You're not betting it all?

618
00:38:45.198 --> 00:38:46.324
All or nothing at all.

619
00:38:46.407 --> 00:38:48.330
Here. Do you want to
throw the dice for me?

620
00:38:48.409 --> 00:38:49.581
No!

621
00:38:50.537 --> 00:38:52.790
Now get ready. Are you ready?

622
00:39:01.589 --> 00:39:03.057
Oh!

623
00:39:06.010 --> 00:39:07.182
I guess that's bad?

624
00:39:07.262 --> 00:39:08.809
Depends on your point of view.

625
00:39:09.055 --> 00:39:11.774
Ooh. look at that.
Come here to Daddy. girl!

626
00:39:12.267 --> 00:39:13.769
All right!
Look at you.

627
00:39:13.893 --> 00:39:17.193
You look great! And that dress!
Gorgeous!

628
00:39:17.856 --> 00:39:19.153
It's on the house.

629
00:39:19.232 --> 00:39:21.392
See? I knew there was a reason
I could afford all this.

630
00:39:21.943 --> 00:39:23.195
Thank you. Shirley!

631
00:39:23.278 --> 00:39:25.451
My father used
to say to me. "Jake...

632
00:39:25.530 --> 00:39:27.908
"Jake. man. you got
two loves in your life.

633
00:39:27.991 --> 00:39:29.493
"What you do and
who you're with."

634
00:39:31.953 --> 00:39:33.079
Happy birthday. Louisa.

635
00:39:33.162 --> 00:39:35.836
- Happy birthday.
- Happy birthday. Louisa!

636
00:39:35.915 --> 00:39:37.462
And a happy New Year.

637
00:39:37.542 --> 00:39:38.794
Happy New Year. everybody!

638
00:39:39.294 --> 00:39:40.796
Happy New Year.
Happy New Year.

639
00:39:41.129 --> 00:39:43.882
Don't go weak in the knees
on me tonight. boy.

640
00:39:43.965 --> 00:39:46.138
You're gonna need all
the strength you got.

641
00:39:46.217 --> 00:39:47.685
- Oh!
- All right. girl.

642
00:39:47.760 --> 00:39:49.762
I knew a one-armed
piano player once.

643
00:39:49.846 --> 00:39:51.940
took two minutes to
play the Minute Waltz.

644
00:39:55.393 --> 00:39:57.121
You know. you oughta watch
how you talk to Michael and I.

645
00:39:57.145 --> 00:39:58.145
We're about to be famous.

646
00:39:58.187 --> 00:39:59.747
Hey. tell 'em about our discovery.
Jake!

647
00:39:59.898 --> 00:40:01.946
No job talk. You promised.

648
00:40:02.358 --> 00:40:03.359
You promised.

649
00:40:04.527 --> 00:40:05.574
Right.

650
00:40:05.653 --> 00:40:08.327
Would you risk
a dance with me. madam?

651
00:40:09.115 --> 00:40:10.162
You'll be sorry.

652
00:40:10.241 --> 00:40:12.539
So will you.
I have two right feet.

653
00:40:12.619 --> 00:40:14.963
That's good.
'cause I have two left.

654
00:40:15.038 --> 00:40:16.790
Well. that's a set.

655
00:40:30.011 --> 00:40:31.934
A little quiet tonight.

656
00:40:32.263 --> 00:40:33.606
New Year's blues?

657
00:40:33.681 --> 00:40:34.978
No. No. not at all.

658
00:40:35.224 --> 00:40:37.977
Come on. It's my party.

659
00:40:38.519 --> 00:40:39.736
He's just Michael.

660
00:40:39.812 --> 00:40:42.691
he's startin' to count them damn
conch in his sleep. you know?

661
00:40:45.026 --> 00:40:46.494
Excuse me.

662
00:40:57.038 --> 00:40:58.255
Mind if I Cut in?

663
00:40:58.331 --> 00:40:59.457
Please.

664
00:40:59.540 --> 00:41:01.634
The world would
be a better place

665
00:41:01.709 --> 00:41:04.337
if more sons danced
with their mothers.

666
00:41:10.385 --> 00:41:12.353
Michael. stop pouting.

667
00:41:12.887 --> 00:41:14.365
You look like you
did when you were six

668
00:41:14.389 --> 00:41:16.938
and didn't get
something you wanted.

669
00:41:17.892 --> 00:41:20.236
I like him.
I enjoy his company-.

670
00:41:20.937 --> 00:41:22.530
Yeah.

671
00:41:22.981 --> 00:41:25.109
I don't like him
chasing around after you.

672
00:41:25.483 --> 00:41:26.700
I don't trust him.

673
00:41:26.776 --> 00:41:28.949
He's not chasing.
I'm not running.

674
00:41:29.028 --> 00:41:30.996
You are being ridiculous.

675
00:41:31.739 --> 00:41:34.538
Look. I've been a pain in
the ass and I'm sorry.

676
00:41:34.617 --> 00:41:36.540
I'm not gonna bother you
anymore about your work.

677
00:41:36.619 --> 00:41:37.763
You're not a pain in the ass.

678
00:41:37.787 --> 00:41:38.834
Come on. let me finish.

679
00:41:38.913 --> 00:41:41.917
I've been rehearsing
this all day.

680
00:41:42.166 --> 00:41:43.268
Your brother's
death almost killed me.

681
00:41:43.292 --> 00:41:45.886
I don't know.
I'll never get over it.

682
00:41:46.170 --> 00:41:49.344
But I refuse to let myself
be run by an obsession.

683
00:41:49.424 --> 00:41:52.394
I can't keep on
believing it was intentional.

684
00:41:53.094 --> 00:41:55.096
I finally figured it out.

685
00:41:56.097 --> 00:41:57.189
Good.

686
00:41:57.890 --> 00:41:59.392
That's it. "Good"?

687
00:41:59.475 --> 00:42:02.194
I thought you'd
break out the champagne.

688
00:42:03.104 --> 00:42:05.072
No. I'm... I'm pleased.

689
00:42:05.398 --> 00:42:08.777
Come on. Show your mother
what a good dancer you are.

690
00:42:20.747 --> 00:42:22.465
Where is everybody?

691
00:42:23.416 --> 00:42:25.009
Down here!

692
00:42:30.131 --> 00:42:32.054
Where is Clarence and William?

693
00:42:32.133 --> 00:42:33.726
I gave them the day off.

694
00:42:33.801 --> 00:42:36.099
What for?
We got a job to finish.

695
00:42:36.179 --> 00:42:37.977
Why are you
making a transmitter?

696
00:42:38.056 --> 00:42:40.525
It's all part of
the master plan. Michael.

697
00:42:40.600 --> 00:42:42.352
We're gonna test
it out right now.

698
00:42:42.435 --> 00:42:45.985
We're gonna learn about its
motor systems. its heart rate.

699
00:42:49.817 --> 00:42:52.536
We're going to study an
animal. a magnificent anima!

700
00:42:52.612 --> 00:42:55.115
No one really
knows that much about.

701
00:42:55.990 --> 00:42:57.458
<i>As the sun slowly
sets in the west.</i>

702
00:42:57.533 --> 00:42:59.877
we bid a fond farewell
to the family of conch.

703
00:42:59.952 --> 00:43:01.750
What the hell are
you talking about?

704
00:43:01.829 --> 00:43:03.829
We write it up. wrap it up
and hand it in. brother.

705
00:43:04.707 --> 00:43:07.227
Hey. how come your heart's so stronger
than mine. You got two of them?

706
00:43:07.251 --> 00:43:09.925
Wait. we don't write up
anything until we're finished.

707
00:43:10.004 --> 00:43:11.648
When I was a small boy.
my father said to me. "Jake...

708
00:43:11.672 --> 00:43:15.347
"Jake. never do anything today
you can put off till tomorrow."

709
00:43:16.511 --> 00:43:18.684
And them conch gonna
be there tomorrow. Michael.

710
00:43:18.763 --> 00:43:20.643
Look. when we got the grant.
it was specified...

711
00:43:20.681 --> 00:43:22.024
No. when I got the grant.

712
00:43:22.100 --> 00:43:23.602
Okay. when I signed on. I...

713
00:43:23.684 --> 00:43:25.231
When I invited you.

714
00:43:25.311 --> 00:43:26.528
We got the grant together.

715
00:43:26.604 --> 00:43:28.231
When we finally got
the grant together.

716
00:43:28.314 --> 00:43:30.167
Look. we got three months'
work left on this thing.

717
00:43:30.191 --> 00:43:33.195
We can't write a report.
We don't know enough.

718
00:43:33.694 --> 00:43:37.039
Michael. we got a rare bird here.
You know that. huh?

719
00:43:37.657 --> 00:43:40.661
Great white don't come down
to the Bahamas. never.

720
00:43:40.743 --> 00:43:41.744
Never.

721
00:43:41.869 --> 00:43:44.213
We supposed to let an opportunity
like that just swim away?

722
00:43:44.288 --> 00:43:45.808
Look. my name goes
on the report. okay?

723
00:43:45.873 --> 00:43:49.719
If it's a half-assed job. I don't get
my doctorate and neither do you.

724
00:43:49.877 --> 00:43:53.632
I thought we were planning a
long. rosy future together. man.

725
00:43:53.881 --> 00:43:55.178
So did I.

726
00:43:58.553 --> 00:44:00.681
Hey! Hey!

727
00:44:01.889 --> 00:44:03.015
Michael.

728
00:44:03.099 --> 00:44:05.318
anybody home in there at all?

729
00:44:05.726 --> 00:44:08.980
Man. you better beam down to
Earth with the rest of us.

730
00:44:09.063 --> 00:44:10.499
Even if that shark's
still in the water.

731
00:44:10.523 --> 00:44:12.651
it's not gonna be
there forever. you know?

732
00:44:12.733 --> 00:44:16.363
It's gonna figure out the water's too warm.
It's gonna swim away.

733
00:44:16.445 --> 00:44:17.492
Look me in the eyes. boy.

734
00:44:17.572 --> 00:44:21.167
Tell me you don't want to study
that fish as much as I do.

735
00:44:22.743 --> 00:44:25.872
Michael? Huh?
This is what we trained for.

736
00:44:26.831 --> 00:44:29.755
This is what we
studied them damn books for.

737
00:44:31.252 --> 00:44:33.004
Remember. my name
goes on that report. too.

738
00:44:33.087 --> 00:44:36.136
It's <i>as</i> important to me
as it is to you. right?

739
00:44:36.215 --> 00:44:37.655
All right.
you like them damn snails?

740
00:44:38.843 --> 00:44:40.937
All right. all right.
I'll make you a deal.

741
00:44:41.012 --> 00:44:42.184
Huh? Listen.

742
00:44:42.722 --> 00:44:45.271
We study that shark.
just for a few days.

743
00:44:45.349 --> 00:44:47.898
and it's back to
your lovely snails.

744
00:44:48.436 --> 00:44:50.939
Now. that's fair. man.
That's fair.

745
00:44:52.064 --> 00:44:54.408
Come on. indulge me with it. eh?

746
00:45:00.072 --> 00:45:01.745
