01:04:08.678 --> 01:04:11.272
Michael. I can't just
let you go back down.

993
01:04:14.225 --> 01:04:15.977
I'm scared shitless.

994
01:04:17.062 --> 01:04:18.122
What the hell am
I supposed to do

995
01:04:18.146 --> 01:04:19.426
if I can't go
back in that water?

996
01:04:22.859 --> 01:04:24.736
All right. be careful.

997
01:04:37.791 --> 01:04:38.893
Clarence. get up on that shack.

998
01:04:38.917 --> 01:04:40.770
Give us some lookout
with them glasses. all right?

999
01:04:40.794 --> 01:04:42.104
I hope the man
knows what he's doing.

1000
01:04:42.128 --> 01:04:45.223
Yeah. well. he's doin'
what he's got to do. eh.

1001
01:05:00.855 --> 01:05:02.778
Jake.
what's the monitor look like?

1002
01:05:02.857 --> 01:05:04.337
Are you gettin'
anything on the shark?

1003
01:05:08.696 --> 01:05:10.573
No. everything's cool.

1004
01:05:10.698 --> 01:05:13.577
You know. I'm thinkin' about yesterday.
It's probably all a mistake.

1005
01:05:13.660 --> 01:05:16.288
<i>He was just hungry. You got
that tasty look. you know?</i>

1006
01:05:16.371 --> 01:05:18.465
Yeah. but how come only me.
though. you know?

1007
01:05:19.124 --> 01:05:20.421
Maybe he just like white meat.

1008
01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:22.718
You're a funny guy. Jake.

1009
01:05:26.589 --> 01:05:27.761
Jesus!

1010
01:05:40.145 --> 01:05:44.366
<i>"It is about
art that I wish to speak today.</i>

1011
01:05:46.359 --> 01:05:49.989
<i>"The raw material of
art surrounds us all.</i>

1012
01:05:50.071 --> 01:05:54.326
<i>"catching in the net that each
and every one of us casts</i>

1013
01:05:54.409 --> 01:05:56.411
<i>"into the current of life.</i>

1014
01:05:57.954 --> 01:05:59.581
<i>"But it takes the art..."</i>

1015
01:05:59.664 --> 01:06:01.632
Where the hell are they?

1016
01:06:02.750 --> 01:06:04.297
They'll be here.

1017
01:06:04.377 --> 01:06:05.497
Can I go on the banana boat?

1018
01:06:06.546 --> 01:06:09.299
Margaret's going.
She's with her mother.

1019
01:06:10.008 --> 01:06:11.100
Okay.

1020
01:06:11.259 --> 01:06:12.351
Oh. boy! Oh. boy!

1021
01:06:12.427 --> 01:06:14.304
Thea. you be careful.

1022
01:06:14.387 --> 01:06:15.889
- I will. I will!
- Thea!

1023
01:06:15.972 --> 01:06:18.270
It's okay.
Banana boats are fun.

1024
01:06:19.559 --> 01:06:23.439
Oh. we should be so lucky-I wish
we were out there with her playin'.

1025
01:06:23.521 --> 01:06:25.398
Margaret. wait for me!

1026
01:06:26.608 --> 01:06:30.488
<i>"Get to the point. man."
as my wife now says.</i>

1027
01:06:33.448 --> 01:06:38.705
<i>Okay. Well. in short. art is
grease for the wheel of life.</i>

1028
01:06:39.704 --> 01:06:44.335
<i>Today. we are privileged
to dedicate a work of art.</i>

1029
01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:47.011
<i>Carla Brody.</i>

1030
01:06:48.213 --> 01:06:51.387
<i>an artist of growing reputation.</i>

1031
01:06:51.466 --> 01:06:56.939
<i>was commissioned to express our
way of life in permanent form</i>

1032
01:06:57.931 --> 01:07:02.232
<i>to show the world what we all
know right here on this beach.</i>

1033
01:07:02.310 --> 01:07:04.984
<i>That it is
better in the Bahamas.</i>

1034
01:07:05.104 --> 01:07:06.481
Absolutely.

1035
01:07:07.398 --> 01:07:11.699
<i>Ladies and gentlemen.
Carla Brody!</i>

1036
01:07:13.488 --> 01:07:16.958
<i>Thank you. Commissioner
Witherspoon. Mrs. Witherspoon.</i>

1037
01:07:25.333 --> 01:07:26.755
Thea!

1038
01:07:33.466 --> 01:07:34.888
Oh. my God!

1039
01:07:37.762 --> 01:07:38.854
Thea!

1040
01:07:39.138 --> 01:07:40.811
Get out of the water!

1041
01:07:40.890 --> 01:07:44.815
Stop!
Come back! Bring her back!

1042
01:07:47.313 --> 01:07:48.485
Oh. my God!

1043
01:08:03.538 --> 01:08:06.087
Stop! Thea! Thea!

1044
01:08:06.332 --> 01:08:07.504
Thea!

1045
01:08:07.917 --> 01:08:09.794
Somebody do something!

1046
01:08:14.882 --> 01:08:16.008
Thea!

1047
01:08:16.134 --> 01:08:18.228
No! No!

1048
01:08:18.344 --> 01:08:20.847
No! Oh. my God!

1049
01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:23.600
Oh! Oh. my God!

1050
01:08:34.861 --> 01:08:36.158
Mommy! Mommy!

1051
01:08:36.279 --> 01:08:37.531
Thea. are you all right?

1052
01:08:40.158 --> 01:08:42.832
Somebody get a doctor!
Get a doctor now!

1053
01:08:44.412 --> 01:08:45.538
Quickly!

1054
01:08:49.334 --> 01:08:50.881
I want my mom!

1055
01:09:52.438 --> 01:09:53.540
Hey. I'm sorry I missed you.

1056
01:09:53.564 --> 01:09:54.565
Where have you been?

1057
01:09:55.608 --> 01:09:56.888
What's the matter?
What happened?

1058
01:09:57.026 --> 01:09:58.744
Thea was attacked by a shark.

1059
01:09:59.362 --> 01:10:00.739
Oh. my God.

1060
01:10:02.073 --> 01:10:05.122
The doctor said she should be all right.
She's in shock.

1061
01:10:06.619 --> 01:10:07.836
Sweetheart? Sweetheart?

1062
01:10:08.162 --> 01:10:10.460
Oh. my God. I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.

1063
01:10:10.540 --> 01:10:11.883
I should've known. Jesus.

1064
01:10:11.958 --> 01:10:13.801
Should've known what?

1065
01:10:18.589 --> 01:10:19.942
We were trying to
keep track of it.

1066
01:10:19.966 --> 01:10:21.764
<i>Of...
The</i> shark.

1067
01:10:22.051 --> 01:10:23.394
The shark?
You knew?

1068
01:10:23.469 --> 01:10:24.641
Yeah. thought it went away.

1069
01:10:24.721 --> 01:10:25.722
Came after me yesterday.

1070
01:10:25.805 --> 01:10:27.978
She could've been killed.
You knew?

1071
01:10:28.349 --> 01:10:30.317
And you didn't tell us?

1072
01:10:30.476 --> 01:10:31.819
You let your mother think...

1073
01:10:31.894 --> 01:10:33.646
Where is she?
How could you do that?

1074
01:10:33.813 --> 01:10:35.360
Where's my mother?
Your own daughter'?

1075
01:10:35.523 --> 01:10:36.740
Where is my mother?

1076
01:10:36.816 --> 01:10:37.988
Why didn't you tell us?

1077
01:10:38.276 --> 01:10:39.402
Where's Jake?

1078
01:10:39.485 --> 01:10:41.408
Why didn't you tell us?

1079
01:10:44.824 --> 01:10:46.167
Michael!

1080
01:10:50.163 --> 01:10:51.289
Jake!

1081
01:10:52.331 --> 01:10:53.332
Jake!

1082
01:10:53.416 --> 01:10:54.588
What?

1083
01:10:54.667 --> 01:10:56.715
Come on! I need you! Hurry up!

1084
01:11:16.898 --> 01:11:19.117
Hoagie! Did you see our boat?

1085
01:11:19.609 --> 01:11:21.111
I just got here.

1086
01:11:21.277 --> 01:11:22.620
My mother took it.

1087
01:11:23.070 --> 01:11:25.118
I hope she's a good sailor.

1088
01:11:25.198 --> 01:11:26.996
A shark attacked
Thea and some kids.

1089
01:11:27.074 --> 01:11:28.917
She went after the damn thing.

1090
01:11:28.993 --> 01:11:30.165
She's gone after it?

1091
01:11:30.411 --> 01:11:32.254
Yeah. we gotta stop her.

1092
01:11:32.538 --> 01:11:34.256
You're going after her in that?

1093
01:11:34.332 --> 01:11:36.209
It'll take all
day in that bathtub.

1094
01:11:36.876 --> 01:11:38.549
You got a better idea. man?

1095
01:11:42.298 --> 01:11:43.720
I'll radio her position.

1096
01:11:43.800 --> 01:11:47.304
And the rescue boats will come
and pick her up. so don't worry.

1097
01:11:47.386 --> 01:11:48.808
She'll be fine. partner.

1098
01:11:48.888 --> 01:11:51.641
She'll never find that bloody
shark. man-We couldn't.

1099
01:11:51.724 --> 01:11:53.567
It'll find her.

1100
01:11:53.643 --> 01:11:55.003
What do you
mean. "it'll find her"?

1101
01:11:55.311 --> 01:11:57.234
She said it was coming.

1102
01:11:57.897 --> 01:11:59.774
What do you mean. "She
said it was coming"?

1103
01:11:59.857 --> 01:12:01.154
What do you know about it?

1104
01:12:01.234 --> 01:12:02.586
Well. she's got
the idea in her head

1105
01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:06.035
that the shark that killed Martin
and Sean is following the family.

1106
01:12:06.113 --> 01:12:08.957
Hey. he's not talkin'
about our shark. eh?

1107
01:12:09.909 --> 01:12:12.788
What do you do when
you're not flying people?

1108
01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:14.543
I deliver laundry.

1109
01:12:16.207 --> 01:12:20.007
Hold on. What's that?
Let's have a look.

1110
01:12:27.552 --> 01:12:28.599
Oh.

1111
01:12:31.472 --> 01:12:33.691
It's a big ocean out there.

1112
01:13:12.138 --> 01:13:13.515
Can't this thing go any faster?

1113
01:13:13.598 --> 01:13:16.602
If I go any faster. this thing'll
turn into a flying Cuisinart

1114
01:13:16.684 --> 01:13:18.561
and we'll be
diced into oblivion.

1115
01:13:47.256 --> 01:13:49.133
Come and get me.
you son of a bitch.

1116
01:13:55.640 --> 01:13:58.063
There she is.
That's her right there.

1117
01:14:00.853 --> 01:14:02.105
Is that what I think it is?

1118
01:14:04.815 --> 01:14:06.488
Mom...
Hold on!

1119
01:14:34.720 --> 01:14:36.097
Thomas. my boy. are you there?

1120
01:14:36.180 --> 01:14:38.182
This is Zero-Papa-Alpha here.

1121
01:14:38.265 --> 01:14:39.812
<i>Hoagie. where the hell are you?</i>

1122
01:14:39.892 --> 01:14:42.566
I'm 12 miles
southeast of Emerald Key.

1123
01:14:42.645 --> 01:14:44.739
<i>Look for</i> a <i>ketch
called Neptune's Folly.</i>

1124
01:14:47.650 --> 01:14:51.905
I need a coupla boats fast and somebody
who can kill a shark. a big one.

1125
01:14:51.988 --> 01:14:53.114
<i>What're you doing?</i>

1126
01:14:53.197 --> 01:14:54.449
I'm practicing landing.

1127
01:14:55.074 --> 01:14:56.792
Hang on to your socks. lads.

1128
01:14:56.867 --> 01:14:59.711
Hey! Wait a minute. man. You
sure you know how to do this?

1129
01:14:59.787 --> 01:15:03.087
Of course not! What kind of
pilot do you think I am?

1130
01:15:18.097 --> 01:15:19.940
Christ!
Hell. that wasn't half bad.

1131
01:15:20.016 --> 01:15:21.814
Get out of here.
I'll keep it busy.

1132
01:15:21.892 --> 01:15:23.235
No. it's gonna
come for the plane.

1133
01:15:23.310 --> 01:15:26.029
It's attracted to the electromagnetic
impulse of the metal on it.

1134
01:15:26.105 --> 01:15:28.449
Get the bloody hell out of here!

1135
01:15:28.774 --> 01:15:29.821
Michael!

1136
01:15:40.411 --> 01:15:44.962
Damn passengers! You're all the same.
Complain. complain...

1137
01:15:45.791 --> 01:15:46.963
Oh. shit!

1138
01:15:49.962 --> 01:15:51.134
Hoagie!

1139
01:15:54.008 --> 01:15:57.012
Hoagie! Hoagie!

1140
01:16:18.240 --> 01:16:20.334
Why...
Why'd you come out here?

1141
01:16:24.205 --> 01:16:25.752
Why'd you come out here?

1142
01:16:25.831 --> 01:16:27.799
Why did you bring him? Why?
Mom. Mom!

1143
01:16:27.875 --> 01:16:29.502
Why'd you take the boat?

1144
01:16:29.585 --> 01:16:31.563
It kept coming! Didn't you
realize what you were doing?

1145
01:16:31.587 --> 01:16:33.840
I had to do it.
There was nothing else to do.

1146
01:16:33.964 --> 01:16:35.244
Mom. you shouldn't have done it.

1147
01:16:35.299 --> 01:16:37.768
I tried to tell you.

1148
01:16:37.843 --> 01:16:39.060
I tried.

1149
01:16:45.601 --> 01:16:48.150
Hey! Give me a hand here.
for Christ's sake!

1150
01:16:48.521 --> 01:16:49.568
Hoagie!

1151
01:16:49.647 --> 01:16:51.570
How the hell did
you do that. man?

1152
01:16:51.649 --> 01:16:53.276
It wasn't easy. believe me.

1153
01:16:53.359 --> 01:16:54.879
Get him up. Get him up.
Quick. Got him!

1154
01:16:56.403 --> 01:16:57.950
Pull him up. Right.

1155
01:16:58.030 --> 01:16:59.782
You all right. man?
Oh!

1156
01:17:00.199 --> 01:17:02.247
Oh! Bloody hell.

1157
01:17:02.326 --> 01:17:04.262
Get it started! Double-time.
The breath on that thing!

1158
01:17:04.286 --> 01:17:05.287
You are alive!

1159
01:17:05.371 --> 01:17:06.372
Oh!

1160
01:17:06.455 --> 01:17:08.799
Let's get out of here.
Ellen Brody. Oh!

1161
01:17:09.959 --> 01:17:11.239
Good.
this thing's still working.

1162
01:17:11.502 --> 01:17:14.722
That's your engine. pal.
I'll have a look at it.

1163
01:17:18.926 --> 01:17:20.724
Oh. shit. he's close. man.

1164
01:17:21.595 --> 01:17:22.687
What is that sound?

1165
01:17:22.847 --> 01:17:24.315
That's the shark's heartbeat.

1166
01:17:24.390 --> 01:17:26.159
Hoagie. see if you can
get that thing finished. man.

1167
01:17:26.183 --> 01:17:27.869
Michael. give me a hand down here. man.
I got an idea.

1168
01:17:27.893 --> 01:17:31.488
We're taking water down here.
Ellen. start pumping here.

1169
01:17:33.399 --> 01:17:36.118
Ellen. get the bilge pump!

1170
01:17:36.193 --> 01:17:37.337
What's going on?
What do you need?

1171
01:17:37.361 --> 01:17:38.755
Take the transmitter
out on one of them radios

1172
01:17:38.779 --> 01:17:39.881
and hook it to this here strobe.

1173
01:17:39.905 --> 01:17:40.997
Just do it!
Just do it!

1174
01:17:41.073 --> 01:17:42.217
We gotta get the engine started!

1175
01:17:42.241 --> 01:17:43.584
Michael. just do it!

1176
01:17:44.535 --> 01:17:45.787
If that shark attacks us again

1177
01:17:45.870 --> 01:17:48.168
we're gonna feed that big
boy a meal he won't forget.

1178
01:17:48.247 --> 01:17:50.375
You better have something
good going over there.

1179
01:17:50.457 --> 01:17:52.255
We've got a rotten hose here.

1180
01:17:52.501 --> 01:17:54.299
There's a spare one
down there somewhere.

1181
01:17:54.378 --> 01:17:55.397
What you wanna do with this?

1182
01:17:55.421 --> 01:17:57.048
I'm riggin' the receiver.
If it works.

1183
01:17:57.131 --> 01:18:00.476
we get it inside that bastard
and then we set it off.

1184
01:18:00.801 --> 01:18:02.519
I got it. I got it. I got it.

1185
01:18:02.595 --> 01:18:04.114
We rig an antenna on this.
we got a slave unit

1186
01:18:04.138 --> 01:18:05.515
that'll shock
the hell out of him.

1187
01:18:05.598 --> 01:18:06.838
Right!
You're learning. partner.

1188
01:18:10.394 --> 01:18:11.646
He's getting closer!

1189
01:18:11.729 --> 01:18:13.731
They spend half their lives
looking for food.

1190
01:18:13.814 --> 01:18:16.693
and the other half eating it.
they don't care what it is.

1191
01:18:16.901 --> 01:18:19.575
Maybe he's got indigestion.
He's already eaten my plane!

1192
01:18:21.739 --> 01:18:23.787
It's not food he's after.

1193
01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:26.498
Michael. turn on your switch.
I wanna get a test here.

1194
01:18:26.577 --> 01:18:28.096
All right. anybody ever tell
you you're nuts?

1195
01:18:28.120 --> 01:18:29.497
All the time. partner.

1196
01:18:29.580 --> 01:18:30.640
This is all theory. though.

1197
01:18:30.664 --> 01:18:32.507
If it responds to external
electrical impulse.

1198
01:18:32.583 --> 01:18:35.006
it might respond
to one coming from inside it.

1199
01:18:35.085 --> 01:18:36.428
Confuse him. drive him crazy.

1200
01:18:36.503 --> 01:18:38.096
All right. give me a test.

1201
01:18:38.631 --> 01:18:39.757
Good.

1202
01:18:43.928 --> 01:18:47.148
You'd better get up here!
The heartbeat's stopped!

1203
01:18:53.312 --> 01:18:54.438
Shit.

1204
01:18:55.105 --> 01:18:58.234
Either he's gone or your
gear's crapped out again.

1205
01:19:00.152 --> 01:19:02.826
No. no. that's bull. man.
My equipment don't crap out.

1206
01:19:02.905 --> 01:19:04.077
He'll be back.

1207
01:19:04.657 --> 01:19:06.500
Get me the boat hook.

1208
01:19:06.784 --> 01:19:08.536
Maybe he had a heart attack.

1209
01:19:08.619 --> 01:19:09.916
Too much bloody food.

1210
01:19:09.995 --> 01:19:11.872
Humans are full of
cholesterol. you know?

1211
01:19:11.956 --> 01:19:13.833
Give me the hook.
Shit! Where the hell is he?

1212
01:19:16.627 --> 01:19:18.550
All right.
give me that line. Michael.

1213
01:19:18.629 --> 01:19:20.006
Right there.

1214
01:19:20.839 --> 01:19:21.840
There he is!

1215
01:19:24.343 --> 01:19:26.220
Ellen. try the engine.

1216
01:19:28.097 --> 01:19:30.441
Ellen. try to start the engine!

1217
01:19:32.851 --> 01:19:33.852
Come on!

1218
01:19:35.354 --> 01:19:37.777
Son of a bitch.
Let's get out of here.

1219
01:19:39.191 --> 01:19:41.285
No. it's too late. Hoagie.
He's gonna come for us.

1220
01:19:41.360 --> 01:19:42.361
Give me a hard port.

1221
01:19:43.153 --> 01:19:44.154
Right!

1222
01:19:44.530 --> 01:19:46.123
Here. give me that.
Come on.

1223
01:19:46.198 --> 01:19:47.791
No. look. this looks
bad here. No!

1224
01:19:47.866 --> 01:19:49.261
Michael. we have no time
for that thing!

1225
01:19:49.285 --> 01:19:52.164
Jake! Jake. you can't go out
there without a line!

1226
01:19:55.457 --> 01:19:57.755
Keep it steady.
It's gonna come back!

1227
01:20:15.894 --> 01:20:18.397
Damn thing's disappeared.
He's gone!

1228
01:20:55.934 --> 01:20:57.777
Jake!

1229
01:21:30.427 --> 01:21:33.055
We're taking too much water.
It'll stop the engine.

1230
01:21:33.138 --> 01:21:36.859
Ellen. take the wheel.
We've got to outrun it. Ellen!

1231
01:21:54.076 --> 01:21:55.328
That thing gonna work?

1232
01:21:56.328 --> 01:21:57.420
It'll work.

1233
01:21:57.496 --> 01:21:59.015
If Jake says it will work.
it will work.

1234
01:21:59.039 --> 01:22:00.666
This kinda charge
will drive it crazy.

1235
01:22:08.215 --> 01:22:10.434
Help!

1236
01:23:05.063 --> 01:23:07.111
Sweet Jesus.
we're headed straight for it!

1237
01:23:07.191 --> 01:23:08.659
Come about. Ellen!

1238
01:23:08.734 --> 01:23:10.532
Ellen. come about!

1239
01:23:16.867 --> 01:23:20.963
He's gonna hit us.
Hold on! Hold on!

1240
01:23:23.248 --> 01:23:25.216
Smile. you son of a bitch!

1241
01:23:50.943 --> 01:23:51.944
Michael!

1242
01:23:52.402 --> 01:23:53.779
Come over here.

1243
01:23:57.616 --> 01:23:58.913
Michael!

1244
01:23:59.868 --> 01:24:01.870
It's all right! I'm okay!

1245
01:24:01.954 --> 01:24:03.046
Anybody alive?

1246
01:24:03.997 --> 01:24:05.123
Over here!

1247
01:24:08.502 --> 01:24:09.754
Jake!

1248
01:24:12.589 --> 01:24:14.637
Michael. you got a minute?

1249
01:24:15.676 --> 01:24:17.144
It's Jake!

1250
01:24:20.973 --> 01:24:22.520
Son of a bitch!

1251
01:24:33.277 --> 01:24:34.699
Jesus. Jake.

1252
01:24:39.324 --> 01:24:41.668
What took you so damn long. man?

1253
01:24:42.911 --> 01:24:44.913
What the hell are
you doing alive. huh?

1254
01:24:44.997 --> 01:24:48.501
I told you... I told you Uncle
Jake's equipment don't crap out. eh?

1255
01:24:52.921 --> 01:24:55.674
You're not going to do something
stupid like die on me. are you?

1256
01:24:56.258 --> 01:24:59.512
No. man.
I'm way too mean for that.

1257
01:25:02.306 --> 01:25:04.058
All right. here you go.

1258
01:25:07.686 --> 01:25:10.189
So from now on. we're going
to study snails. eh?

1259
01:25:10.272 --> 01:25:11.444
Yeah.

1260
01:25:17.029 --> 01:25:19.532
I want you all to come
to Amity this summer.

1261
01:25:19.615 --> 01:25:20.787
Yeah. we'll be there.

1262
01:25:20.866 --> 01:25:22.368
You make sure they come.

1263
01:25:22.451 --> 01:25:25.204
I will.
I'll miss you. Grandma.

1264
01:25:27.956 --> 01:25:30.209
Get in. Ellen Brody.
You'll miss your plane.

1265
01:25:30.292 --> 01:25:31.919
Goodbye. Grandma!
Bye. baby.

1266
01:25:32.002 --> 01:25:33.379
Okay.
Be careful.

1267
01:25:33.462 --> 01:25:35.089
Okay. See ya.

1268
01:25:36.298 --> 01:25:37.720
Take good care of Jake.

1269
01:25:37.799 --> 01:25:39.016
I will.

1270
01:25:40.218 --> 01:25:41.891
You gonna be okay?

1271
01:25:42.971 --> 01:25:44.143
Yeah.

1272
01:25:44.765 --> 01:25:45.891
Okay.

1273
01:25:47.726 --> 01:25:50.354
When I come back. remind me
to tell you about the time

1274
01:25:50.437 --> 01:25:52.781
I took 100 nuns to Nairobi.

1275
01:25:58.654 --> 01:26:02.454
There they were.
100 nuns. playing guitars

1276
01:26:02.532 --> 01:26:06.127
and singing. "The hills are
alive with the sound of music."

1277
01:26:06.203 --> 01:26:10.333
Then suddenly. one comes
up to me and she <i>says.</i>

1278
01:26:10.415 --> 01:26:13.294
"There's smoke
coming from the engine."

1279
01:26:13.377 --> 01:26:15.220
But I never took them seriously.

1280
01:26:15.295 --> 01:26:19.095
until they all started singing
Nearer. <i>My</i> God. to Thee.

